Anime streaming service Crunchyroll is <a href="https://help.crunchyroll.com/hc/en-us/articles/46192117514132-Crunchyroll-Apple-TV-Channel">now available</a> as an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app channel, making it easier for prospective customers to subscribe without having to open up another app.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/crunchyroll-apple-tv-channels.jpg" alt="" width="1372" height="772" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1042920" /><br/>
&zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; users in the U.S., Canada, UK, and Australia are now able to subscribe to Crunchyroll through the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj;. There's a 7-day free trial available, after which the service is priced at &#36;9.99 per month. The Crunchyroll &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; Channel is separate from existing Crunchyroll subscriptions, and an existing account can't be linked to the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app.<br/>
<br/>
As with all &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; Channels content, if you sign up for Crunchyroll with the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app, you'll be billed through Apple. Crunchyroll says its full catalog of over 50,000 episodes is available through the Crunchyroll &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; Channel.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://tv.apple.com/us/room/explore-channels-on-apple-tv/edt.item.5c8d632b-c237-4492-9291-540042548797">Apple TV Channels</a> have long been an &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app feature that makes subscribing to multiple services more convenient. Channels content can be watched in the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app without having to open up another app, and access can be shared with up to six members of a Family Sharing group. Channels also offer watch on-demand content and offline downloads.<br/>
<br/>
